WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.789 --> 00:00:07.240
Speaker 1: . Now it is time for Joe Biden
to get something else done.

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:12.990
Now, if you look at Joe Biden's first 100
day accomplishments, they are significant.

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:18.660
They aren't all exactly the accomplishments
that the progressive left would want.

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:23.340
There are other things we would like for him
to have promised and be working on and ideally

00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:24.880
have done.

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:28.990
But it can't be denied that it was an extremely
productive first 100 days.

00:00:28.990 --> 00:00:33.790
I believe it is now time to move ahead without
Republicans because they simply are not willing

00:00:33.790 --> 00:00:37.250
to participate, probably in the infrastructure
bill.

00:00:37.250 --> 00:00:42.760
And Senator Bernie Sanders of Vermont is now
urging Democrats pushed through the infrastructure

00:00:42.760 --> 00:00:45.320
package without any Republican support.

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:46.320
Just do it.

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:48.420
Bernie was interviewed by ACOSS.

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:56.460
This aired last night, I believe, and he disagreed
with the perspective of some Democratic strategists,

00:00:56.460 --> 00:01:01.410
which is that Republicans must be part of
the deal that Democrats strike if Democrats

00:01:01.410 --> 00:01:03.660
are going to pass the sweeping infrastructure
package.

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:05.880
Bernie said, quote, In general, I don't agree
with that.

00:01:05.880 --> 00:01:08.550
The bottom line is the American people want
results.

00:01:08.550 --> 00:01:13.840
And Bernie said that voters, when it came
to the one point nine dollars billion stimulus,

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:14.840
nobody.

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:16.500
I mean, listen, you can find some people,
right?

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:20.180
If you go to like the villages in Florida
and we will have video from that over the

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:25.260
weekend, you can probably find some people
who say, I was mad at the cash I got.

00:01:25.260 --> 00:01:29.570
From Biden, because no, no Republicans voted
for it, you can find it to a country of three

00:01:29.570 --> 00:01:35.080
hundred and thirty one million, but big picture,
you don't have a wave of opposition to the

00:01:35.080 --> 00:01:40.560
fact that people got money in March or whenever
it was passed because no Republican supported

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:41.560
that.

00:01:41.560 --> 00:01:44.450
And maybe even some Republicans are going
to suffer the electoral consequences of that

00:01:44.450 --> 00:01:45.480
come 2022.

00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:48.841
And Bernie is saying essentially the same
thing, which is what we've been saying, what

00:01:48.841 --> 00:01:50.170
many have been saying.

00:01:50.170 --> 00:01:52.310
The infrastructure bill is popular.

00:01:52.310 --> 00:01:57.500
The infrastructure bill is popular with almost
all Democrats and the majority of independents

00:01:57.500 --> 00:01:59.470
and many Republicans.

00:01:59.470 --> 00:02:04.409
If Republicans really want to dig their heels
in or stick their head in the sand or whatever

00:02:04.409 --> 00:02:09.819
metaphor or analogy you want to use and take
the political risk of all voting against something

00:02:09.819 --> 00:02:15.360
that Americans widely support, want and believe
that we need and that will be economically

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:16.360
stimulative.

00:02:16.360 --> 00:02:19.650
The infrastructure plan let Republicans all
vote against it.

00:02:19.650 --> 00:02:24.650
Mitch McConnell has already said Democrats
will have zero votes on this infrastructure

00:02:24.650 --> 00:02:27.019
package as written.

00:02:27.019 --> 00:02:29.980
We know there's not going to be zero Republican
support.

00:02:29.980 --> 00:02:37.340
Why negotiate into something that will end
up being a garbage bill when even if you do

00:02:37.340 --> 00:02:40.450
that, you may get and are likely to get zero
Republican votes?

00:02:40.450 --> 00:02:42.959
So it's really a simple question.

00:02:42.959 --> 00:02:46.400
Is Joe Biden committed to doing infrastructure
in twenty twenty one?

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:48.829
It's a really simple decision tree.

00:02:48.829 --> 00:02:53.019
If no, then there's then there's 10 options.

00:02:53.019 --> 00:02:54.909
Negotiate in bad with bad faith.

00:02:54.909 --> 00:02:58.799
Republicans water the bill down, postpone
it till 2022.

00:02:58.799 --> 00:02:59.799
Right.

00:02:59.799 --> 00:03:03.639
I mean, if the answer is no, we're not committed
to getting it passed this year.

00:03:03.639 --> 00:03:04.730
The world is your oyster.

00:03:04.730 --> 00:03:06.560
Go do whatever the hell you want.

00:03:06.560 --> 00:03:11.779
If the answer is yes, we're committed to passing
it this year, then you just have to pass it

00:03:11.779 --> 00:03:13.609
without Republican support.

00:03:13.609 --> 00:03:19.749
As much as there is some risk to Democrats
passing another major bill with no Republican

00:03:19.749 --> 00:03:23.541
support, I believe the risk is greater for
Republicans when the bills are popular, when

00:03:23.541 --> 00:03:28.220
the American people don't really care whether
if they think the things should be done.

00:03:28.220 --> 00:03:32.489
Most of the American people are not doing
this inside the Beltway stuff of, oh, I don't

00:03:32.489 --> 00:03:33.489
know.

00:03:33.489 --> 00:03:36.639
I mean, like if if Mitch McConnell had voted
for it, then I'd feel much better about accepting

00:03:36.639 --> 00:03:37.839
my fourteen hundred dollars.

00:03:37.839 --> 00:03:40.689
That basically doesn't exist other than anecdotally.

00:03:40.689 --> 00:03:42.629
So I think the risk is greater for the Republicans.

00:03:42.629 --> 00:03:44.769
Now, there is a practical question.

00:03:44.769 --> 00:03:52.079
It is not totally clear whether Democratic
Senators Joe Manchin and Kirsten Sinema want

00:03:52.079 --> 00:03:54.489
the infrastructure bill passed as written.

00:03:54.489 --> 00:03:58.260
Manchin has already played coy with this idea
of bipartisanship with bad faith.

00:03:58.260 --> 00:04:01.939
Actors who have no interest in what you're
doing is also a question mark.

00:04:01.939 --> 00:04:07.949
So without a doubt, Bernie's plan only works
if you have every Democratic senator on board.

00:04:07.949 --> 00:04:12.249
But there is no question that it's time to
do it and it must be done without Republican

00:04:12.249 --> 00:04:14.120
support because you're not going to get Republican
support.

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:15.590
Mitch McConnell has said it.

00:04:15.590 --> 00:04:19.959
If Mitch McConnell wants to obstruct, let
him do it, but get things done.

00:04:19.959 --> 00:04:26.840
I would rather if I were Joe Biden, I would
rather potentially suffer the consequences

00:04:26.840 --> 00:04:31.660
for doing things without Republicans than
suffer the consequences for not getting a

00:04:31.660 --> 00:04:33.310
damn thing done.

00:04:33.310 --> 00:04:36.070
I think Joe Biden prefers the former as well.

00:04:36.070 --> 00:04:39.680
And we're going to we're going to see very
soon if they decide to go ahead with this

